234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (Bangladesh's air pollution problem is still a serious problem, particularly in large cities like Dhaka and Chittagong. Oftentimes, lists of the most polluted cities in the world include Dhaka. According to recent research, 20% of the nation's premature fatalities are attributable to air pollution. Particulate matter \(PM2.5 and PM10\), carbon monoxide \(CO\), nitrogen dioxide \(NO2\), and sulfur dioxide \(SO2\) are examples of important pollutants. In general, things like automobile emissions, industrial discharges, and construction activities worsen air pollution in Bangladesh. Strict legislative actions and public awareness initiatives are needed to reduce the health concerns linked to poor air quality in order to reduce this pollution.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (Air Campus, a campaign related to air pollution has raised awareness about the severe health and environmental impacts of polluted air, which is a significant cause of premature deaths and chronic diseases. This campaign has educated the public on the sources of air pollution, such as vehicle emissions, industrial discharges, and burning of fossil fuels, and advocated for behavioral changes and policy measures to reduce pollution levels. Being a public awareness campaign, it has mobilized community action and encouraged the adoption of cleaner technology.It was an effective campaign as has lead to substantial improvements in air quality and overall public health, as well as contributed to global efforts to combat climate change by reducing greenhouse gas emissions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 136 0 R
/T (GOALS)
/E (GOALS)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (The Air Campus Campaign is a vital initiative aimed at raising awareness about air pollution and its detrimental effects on health and the environment. Their primary goal is to engage and educate at least 2,000,000 individuals across the nation through this campaign. By leveraging both online and offline channels, they aim to create a broad-reaching impact that inspires action and behavioral change towards improving air quality. Building on our initial success, where they reached 40,000 individuals online in just 15 days, they aim to maintain and accelerate this momentum. By maintaining a consistent and impactful awareness campaign, they envision a future where the entire country is well-informed about air pollution issues and is actively participating in efforts to mitigate it. They plan to hold an air strike movement with the students to make to promote their campaign and make more people engage with air pollution. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
