/T (PARTICIPANTS DEMOGRAPHY )
/E (PARTICIPANTS DEMOGRAPHY )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 141 0 R
/T (The Air Campus campaign successfully reached a diverse demographic, engaging individuals from various age groups, occupational backgrounds, and geographic locations. Initially, school and college-going kids were targeted for the campaign because young minds can do a lot of wonders for society. The children present in the offline and online sessions were between the age of 12-18 years. But it did not stop there. The team worked with university students between 20-24 years. Even the laborers of 20-40 years were also included in the campaign. So the Air Campus campaign was a campaign for all. The campaign is a nationwide initiative designed to engage individuals of all ages and backgrounds in the fight against air pollution. The efforts have spanned across various cities, with a primary focus on Rajshahi and Dhaka. The campaign extended to all corners of the country, ensuring widespread awareness and involvement. Extensive activities, including school visits and community engagements, were conducted in Rajshahi. Primary and Secondary School Students were engaged through interactive workshops, classroom activities, and educational programs in Rajshahi and through online sessions in Dhaka. The team also collaborated with university students across the country, focusing on research, awareness campaigns, and community projects related to air quality improvement. They reached out through workplace visits and community centers, providing practical advice and resources on reducing exposure to harmful pollutants. This awareness campaign also kept going on social media. The facebook impressions reach is also 40k and the organic reach is about 20k in just 15 days. And the response rate is 100%. The ratio of male and female participants were also kept in mind during the campaign. The majority of the air ambassadors are female. In offline and online sessions about 65% were female participants and 35% were male. And on Facebook about 65.8% were men and 34.2% were women. There were almost 10k interactions.)
/E (The Air Campus campaign successfully reached a diverse demographic, engaging individuals from various age groups, occupational backgrounds, and geographic locations. Initially, school and college-going kids were targeted for the campaign because young minds can do a lot of wonders for society. The children present in the offline and online sessions were between the age of 12-18 years. But it did not stop there. The team worked with university students between 20-24 years. Even the laborers of 20-40 years were also included in the campaign. So the Air Campus campaign was a campaign for all. The campaign is a nationwide initiative designed to engage individuals of all ages and backgrounds in the fight against air pollution. The efforts have spanned across various cities, with a primary focus on Rajshahi and Dhaka. The campaign extended to all corners of the country, ensuring widespread awareness and involvement. Extensive activities, including school visits and community engagements, were conducted in Rajshahi. Primary and Secondary School Students were engaged through interactive workshops, classroom activities, and educational programs in Rajshahi and through online sessions in Dhaka. The team also collaborated with university students across the country, focusing on research, awareness campaigns, and community projects related to air quality improvement. They reached out through workplace visits and community centers, providing practical advice and resources on reducing exposure to harmful pollutants. This awareness campaign also kept going on social media. The facebook impressions reach is also 40k and the organic reach is about 20k in just 15 days. And the response rate is 100%. The ratio of male and female participants were also kept in mind during the campaign. The majority of the air ambassadors are female. In offline and online sessions about 65% were female participants and 35% were male. And on Facebook about 65.8% were men and 34.2% were women. There were almost 10k interactions.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
