/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (The first infographic delves into the harmful effects of air pollution on health. It outlines short-term impacts such as asthma,allergy etc and long-term consequences like chronic respiratory diseases, cardiovascular problems, and reduced life expectancy. It was mostly to make people aware of the effects of air pollution. The second infographic highlights the alarming air quality in Dhaka. It presents data on the high levels of particulate matter 2.5. This shows the alarming situation of air pollution. The third infographic provides a sobering look at the life expectancy lost due to air pollution, comparing data from various countries.The fourth infographic presents a global air quality report, ranking the world's most polluted cities. New Delhi, India, tops the list, closely followed by cities in Bangladesh. This is to make people aware of this silent killer. The fifth infographic suggests practical measures individuals can take to improve air quality. Recommendations include using air purifiers, encouraging cycling over driving, wearing masks to reduce inhalation of pollutants, and planting trees to enhance air quality. This shows the way people can be safe from the health effects. The sixth infographic focuses on the air quality situation within Bangladesh, showing a map of various districts. The seventh infographic highlights the economic burden of air pollution, showing that nearly a trillion dollars are lost annually due to health care costs, lost labor productivity and other economic impacts. The eighth infographic analyzes daily air quality patterns in Dhaka. It reveals that the worst air quality is typically observed between 3 to 11 AM, while the best periods are from 3 to 6 AM and 9 to 11 PM. The ninth infographic compares indoor and outdoor air pollution, highlighting that indoor pollution is a significant health threat, causing approximately 74,000 deaths annually. It stresses the importance of addressing indoor air quality alongside outdoor pollution. The tenth infographic details the major pollutants, including PM2.5, PM10, nitrogen dioxide \(NO2\), sulfur dioxide \(SO2\), and carbon monoxide \(CO\), and their effects on human health and the environment. The eleventh infographic identifies the )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
